I confirmed both weakened explanation cases with **in-memory probes**: missing explanations still passed the replacement choice-preview checks.

There is also a separate test defect at **`packs-review-settings.mjs:289`**: `!sec()` invokes a helper that navigates away from the paths page. I reproduced the false assertion and navigation; the following assertion then encounters a missing paths page, preventing later path/stale tests from completing.

One inherited coverage limit remains: backup count is checked only after the first UI Save (`:262`), and the refreshed-path Save (`:336`) lacks an apply-count assertion. Extra writes/backups specifically there could escape detection.

No files changed; full suites were not run.
